    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "If $x+y=5$ and $xy=7$, find the value of $x^2+y^2$ without attempting to find $x$ or $y$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$11$\n\nUse the square-of-a-sum identity and subtract $2xy$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+y^2&=(x+y)^2-2xy\\\\x^2+y^2&=5^2-2(7)\\\\x^2+y^2&=25-14\\\\x^2+y^2&=11\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
